```

In this code, the program checks if the given index is valid (within the range of command-line arguments). If it's valid, the argument at that index is printed to the screen using `printf`. This function takes care of converting a string to an integer using the built-in function `atoi()` and implementing the functionality of the atoi() function from the C standard library.

